WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.159 --> 00:00:03.148
Mind Your Decisions, I'm Presh Talwalkar

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:08.609
In a rectangle, inscribe a semicircle along one of its sides

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:14.250
Then, inscribe a circle that's tangent to both the semicircle and the rectangle

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:19.799
If the semicircle has a radius equal to a and the circle has a radius equal to b

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:26.939
What is the value of a divided by b? I thank Manoj and Katlego for the suggestion

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:33.389
Pause if you'd like to give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching to learn how to solve this problem

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:52.409
First, recall that if two circles are tangent their centers and the tangent point are collinear

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:57.419
This is because each circles' radius is perpendicular to the tangent line

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:06.460
Therefore, ACB will be a straight line segment. This is true for both externally and internally tangent circles

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:14.100
Now, to solve the problem, connect the center of the semicircle, the tangent point and the center of the inscribed circle

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:24.260
Notice, this will be a radius of the small circle and we will  also create a radius of the small circle by creating the tangent line to the other side of the rectangle

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:30.540
The bottom left corner is a square. If we extend the diagonal of the square

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:35.580
to the corner of the rectangle, It will also be collinear with the line we just created.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:40.740
Therefore we've created an isosceles right triangle where two legs are equal to b

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.380
and the hypotenuse is equal to b times the square root of 2

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:50.399
The radius of the semicircle is equal to a and therefore we have another isosceles right triangle

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:53.489
So its hypotenuse will be equal to a times the square root of 2

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:57.479
Notice, we also have a radius of the semicircle right here

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:03.540
We'll now focus on just these triangles and in particular, we'll focus just on the hypotenuse

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:07.830
The entire hypotenuse has a length equal to a times the square root of 2

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:12.479
It also has a length equal to the sum of these individual lengths

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:17.069
This will be equal to a plus b plus b times the square root of 2

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:23.010
We then subtract a from both sides of the equation. We then factor on both sides

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:28.499
We then divide both sides by b and both sides by the square root of 2 minus 1

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:33.700
We thus get that a divided by b is equal to the square root of 2 plus 1 all over

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:41.300
The square root of 2 minus 1 which is approximately equal to 5.828, and that's the answer

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:45.080
It's a cute little problem and I think it's fun to solve

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:53.450
Thanks for making Mind Your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube. As always, thanks for watching and thanks for your support

